# stream.eden.art on the PRODUCTION host (#4159): the worlds' public streams and histories, the same `/s/*` files soul.game
# serves, under a hostname in the eden.art zone, which is behind Cloudflare. The CDN keeps them by its cache rule for
# this host (docs/operations/cdn.md, "The stream hostname") and asks this host once per file, so viewers no longer reach
# the origin one by one. Installed as /etc/caddy/sites/stream-eden-art.caddy; it touches no other site. Until the
# eden.art record points here, Caddy cannot get a certificate for the name and retries with back-off; nothing else is
# affected. The page reads here only when the origin's SOULS_STREAM_ORIGIN names this host.
#
# - /s/* goes to the viewers' origin on 7320 without the /s, exactly as on soul.game; its answers carry their own
#   Cache-Control and Access-Control-Allow-Origin, so nothing is added here.
# - Everything else is a 404 the CDN never keeps: no page, no API, no socket lives on this host.
https://stream.eden.art {
	header X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
	handle_path /s/* {
		reverse_proxy localhost:7320
	}
	handle {
		header Cache-Control no-store
		respond 404
	}
}
